2️⃣ Using requests + BeautifulSoup to Scrape Bing

This is faster than Selenium, but Bing may block your IP after repeated use.

Install Dependencies:

pip install requests beautifulsoup4

Python Code for Bing Search:

import requests
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup

def bing_search(query, max_results=3):
    headers = {
        "User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/91.0.4472.124 Safari/537.36"
    }
    response = requests.get(f"https://www.bing.com/search?q={query.replace(' ', '+')}", headers=headers)
    
    soup = BeautifulSoup(response.text, "html.parser")
    results = []
    
    for result in soup.select("li.b_algo")[:max_results]:
        title = result.select_one("h2").text
        url = result.select_one("h2 a")["href"]
        snippet = result.select_one(".b_caption p").text if result.select_one(".b_caption p") else ""
        results.append({"title": title, "url": url, "snippet": snippet})

    return results

# Run search
results = bing_search("latest AI trends")
for res in results:
    print(f"Title: {res['title']}\nURL: {res['url']}\nSnippet: {res['snippet']}\n")

✅ Pros: Faster, no browser needed
❌ Cons: Bing may detect scraping and block your IP (use proxies if needed)


