3️⃣ Use Startpage (Google Proxy) for Anonymous Search

Startpage is a privacy-focused search engine that fetches Google results anonymously. This avoids Google CAPTCHA blocks.

Install Dependencies:

pip install requests beautifulsoup4

Python Code for Startpage Search:

import requests
from bs4 import BeautifulSoup

def startpage_search(query, max_results=3):
    url = f"https://www.startpage.com/sp/search?q={query.replace(' ', '+')}"
    headers = {"User-Agent": "Mozilla/5.0"}
    response = requests.get(url, headers=headers)
    
    soup = BeautifulSoup(response.text, "html.parser")
    results = []
    
    for result in soup.select(".w-gl__result")[:max_results]:
        title = result.select_one(".w-gl__title").text
        url = result.select_one(".w-gl__result-url").text
        snippet = result.select_one(".w-gl__description").text
        results.append({"title": title, "url": url, "snippet": snippet})

    return results

# Run search
results = startpage_search("latest AI trends")
for res in results:
    print(f"Title: {res['title']}\nURL: {res['url']}\nSnippet: {res['snippet']}\n")

✅ Pros: Uses Google results, but avoids blocks
❌ Cons: Not as widely tested as Bing or DuckDuckGo


